<title>JAPAN: Keisei Electric continues to slip.</title>
<headline>Keisei Electric continues to slip.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Keisei Electric Railway Co Ltd continued to slide on Thursday morning, mainly due to individual investors' loss-cut sales, brokers said.</p>
<p>Those who had hoped for heavy buying in Oriental Land Co Ltd's shares on its debut on Wednesday were disappointed, leading to sales of Keisei Electric, which is a large shareholder in the operator of Tokyo Disneyland.</p>
<p>The share price was down 21 yen at 839 yen at 0056 GMT, in a volume of 2.016 million shares.</p>
